 17592186045417] [17592186347873 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9873e119-5653-5fff-9565-620b8e2698f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345473 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345541 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186345997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186346794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186347053 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186345997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186347881 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "9ea9fa5e-7580-5121-9429-ea3965fd0aec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348333 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347633 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348333 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80117" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348333 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348333 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(5,4,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x-3y+6z=-18.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348333 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ee857b14-a370-505a-a029-ad7460463ae5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348333 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-3y+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6(1)-3(2)+6z & =-18 \\\\ 6z & =-18 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,2,-3⟩-⟨5,4,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,-3,6⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-4)\\cdot 6+(-2)\\cdot (-3)+1\\cdot 6|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-24+6+6|}{\\sqrt{36+9+36}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,-12\\,|}{\\sqrt{81}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348336 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186347873 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348336 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80120" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348336 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348336 #edb/ref 1071 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-11,-8,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $14x+8y-8z=-6.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348336 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "32d1647f-476a-5352-bcda-228c154bf2db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186348336 #edb/ref 1074 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=-1$ and $y=-2$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}14x+8y-8z & =-6 \\\\ 14(-1)+8(-2)-8z & =-6 \\\\ -8z & =24 \\\\ z & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(-1,-2,-3)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨-1,-2,-3⟩-⟨-11,-8,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,6,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨14,8,-8⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot 14+6\\cdot 8+1\\cdot (-8)|}{\\sqrt{(14)^{2}+{8}^{2}+(-8)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|140+48-8|}{\\sqrt{196+64+64}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,180\\,|}{\\sqrt{324}} \\\\  & =10\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365886 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365887 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365888 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186365889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186365885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365884 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d7ca0aa0-a220-5bdc-b0d2-65b3a735f48d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{15}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365885 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "59951a54-81a6-5810-af8e-c4fdad49ec94" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365886 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{18}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365886 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365886 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a90ec159-7db0-5edb-89ff-ff9b5943472c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365887 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{61}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365887 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365887 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fb5bdcd7-37da-5f22-aead-d95e3ecf08f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186365888 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref